/-!
# Borel model factors and literal left source chief refinements

The marked Borel has the actual upper-root two-core. Its fixed F₄-line and
literal natural quotient are irreducible noncentral binary planes, both for
the Borel and for its S₅ normalizer. SourceCoordinates retains the original
qH map, U/V₁ epimorphism and dual-natural embedding into Q_H/C_H(U).
The annihilator flag gives the two dual factors, and additive F₄ coordinates
give the one core conjugation factor. These flags lift to actual chief
refinements under any surjective actor map to the Borel or its normalizer.

SourceChief supplies the conditional 2+2+1 family on the original sections,
including count bounds for every chief series of those intervals. The core
numerator is identified with the actual O₂(L₁T), over the original Q_H.
CompatibleBorel, SectionCentralizer, the earlier source duality and the
commutator identity remain explicit. The SectionCentralizer adapter, compatible
marking, final concatenation and residual comparison for Aschbacher–Smith
14.7.70 (printed p.1074/PDF p.1091) remain with
qt-14-07-rechoice-left-chief-factors. This conditional family does not by
itself complete that source theorem.
-/
